I've recommend gold based on the following loop: Rising federal deficits → higher inflation → rising bond yields → a weaker economy → rising federal deficits. The cycle repeats until asset prices collapse, leaving the Fed to choose between a financial or a currency crisis.

@AnthonyLButler2 No, as inflation more than eats up the real value of the yield. Gold is the best way to hedge against that loss or purchasing power.

@wallstreetboyj Yes, as the financial crisis not only means that bank's fail, with no bailouts, but that the U.S. government defaults on Treasuries, Social Security, and pension obligations. So that seems politically unlikely.
